1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:03,878
<i>Without further ado,</i>
<i>let me introduce to you</i>

2
00:00:03,962 --> 00:00:07,257
<i>the most talented, the most handsome,</i>

3
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:09,801
<i>Jordan Valentin!</i>

4
00:00:09,884 --> 00:00:12,345
[APPLAUSE, CHEERING]

5
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:15,390
♪ <i>I got lost again</i> ♪

6
00:00:15,473 --> 00:00:19,436
♪ <i>Like I learned nothing before</i> ♪

7
00:00:20,478 --> 00:00:23,565
♪ <i>If there are challenges</i> ♪

8
00:00:23,648 --> 00:00:26,735
<i>♪ Save this feeling and help me ♪</i>

9
00:00:26,818 --> 00:00:28,528
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

10
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:30,071
♪ <i>My muse</i> ♪

11
00:00:30,655 --> 00:00:35,994
<i>- </i>♪ <i>Where's our destination?</i> ♪
- [CROWD CHEERING]

12
00:00:36,077 --> 00:00:38,329
♪ <i>You are the captain</i> ♪

13
00:00:38,413 --> 00:00:42,542
♪ <i>I'll follow wherever you go</i> ♪

14
00:00:42,625 --> 00:00:43,460
♪ <i>Oh, baby</i> ♪

15
00:00:43,543 --> 00:00:48,548
<i>- ♪ I'll ride your wave… ♪</i>
- [CROWD CHEERING]

16
00:00:48,631 --> 00:00:50,842
<i>What are you doing here?!</i>

17
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,470
<i>Don't do anything stupid.</i>

18
00:00:53,553 --> 00:00:55,346
<i>Let's go outside. Come on!</i>

19
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:57,932
[CROWD CHEERING]

20
00:00:58,016 --> 00:01:01,061
[DINO] <i>Hurting someone in front of</i>
<i>so many people? Are you insane?!</i>

21
00:01:01,144 --> 00:01:02,604
<i>Who was your target there?</i>

22
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:04,355
<i>Jordan.</i>

23
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:09,694
<i>I didn't know he was your son.</i>
<i>That jerk did me wrong.</i>

24
00:01:09,778 --> 00:01:11,946
<i>Don't you dare hurt Jordan.</i>

25
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:14,574
<i>If you lay a finger on him,</i>
<i>you'll answer to me.</i>

26
00:01:14,657 --> 00:01:16,326
<i>I'm glad that the crowd still loved it</i>

27
00:01:16,409 --> 00:01:18,787
<i>even though it wasn't</i>
<i>your best performance.</i>

28
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:20,997
<i>You seemed distracted earlier.</i>

29
00:01:21,956 --> 00:01:23,708
<i>Is it because of Billy again?</i>

30
00:01:23,792 --> 00:01:25,543
<i>What does she expect?</i>

31
00:01:25,627 --> 00:01:28,880
<i>That we won't sleep</i>
<i>until LoveList improves?</i>

32
00:01:29,464 --> 00:01:32,258
<i>Val, she's just doing her job.</i>

33
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:33,384
<i>She's the CEO.</i>

34
00:01:34,427 --> 00:01:37,472
<i>It's her job to make sure</i>
<i>the company succeeds.</i>

35
00:01:37,555 --> 00:01:40,350
<i>Not to please everyone, not to be nice.</i>

36
00:01:40,433 --> 00:01:42,894
<i>Sometimes, she has to put her foot down.</i>

37
00:01:42,977 --> 00:01:44,854
<i>Besides, it's for our benefit.</i>

38
00:01:44,938 --> 00:01:46,105
[VALERIE] <i>Fine.</i>

39
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:49,400
[CELL PHONE CHIMES]

40
00:01:52,946 --> 00:01:58,743
LOVELIST NEVER RUNS OUT
OF CONTROVERSIES, RIGHT?

41
00:02:04,874 --> 00:02:11,548
TO THE CEO, DO US ALL A FAVOR
AND SHUT IT DOWN!

42
00:02:11,631 --> 00:02:14,884
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

43
00:02:14,968 --> 00:02:16,970
<i>We'll get out of here, Ma.</i>

44
00:02:18,096 --> 00:02:20,140
<i>We'll rise up from this.</i>

45
00:02:20,974 --> 00:02:23,351
<i>And if you still love Papa,</i>

46
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:26,729
<i>I'll take him back for you.</i>

47
00:02:29,941 --> 00:02:36,948
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

48
00:02:41,161 --> 00:02:42,328
<i>Dear?</i>

49
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:47,500
<i>Dad.</i>

50
00:02:47,584 --> 00:02:51,337
<i>I'm sorry I put you through all that.</i>

51
00:02:51,421 --> 00:02:54,632
<i>I should be blamed for what happened</i>
<i>to your sister, not you.</i>

52
00:02:56,968 --> 00:02:58,678
<i>Thank you for understanding.</i>

53
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:02,056
<i>I should be the one thanking you.</i>

54
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:05,268
<i>Get some rest, Dad.</i>

55
00:03:05,852 --> 00:03:07,687
<i>- Good night.</i>
<i>- Good night.</i>

56
00:03:07,770 --> 00:03:14,110
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

57
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:27,957
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

58
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:30,019
You know what, Caloy?

59
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:33,064
You'll be back behind bars
if that happens.

60
00:04:34,649 --> 00:04:35,692
[CHUCKLES]

61
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:38,236
I know.

62
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:41,739
Dino has a point.

63
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:43,950
I'll get in trouble

64
00:04:44,033 --> 00:04:47,537
if I shoot that bastard
right in front of his bar.

65
00:04:48,037 --> 00:04:49,998
Look at that. You know it too.

66
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:53,835
That's why you should turn over a new leaf
and stop that already.

67
00:04:53,918 --> 00:04:55,712
[CHUCKLES SARCASTICALLY]
Turn over a new leaf?

68
00:04:56,379 --> 00:05:01,259
Says the person who fakes IDs,
passports, and other documents.

69
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:03,720
Well? [CHUCKLES]

70
00:05:03,803 --> 00:05:05,054
You're one to talk.

71
00:05:05,138 --> 00:05:06,764
I'm different from you.

72
00:05:07,807 --> 00:05:09,350
I've never hurt anybody!

73
00:05:09,434 --> 00:05:11,185
I don't want to kill anyone.

74
00:05:11,269 --> 00:05:13,479
[WILFRED SIGHS, CLICKS TONGUE]

75
00:05:14,647 --> 00:05:16,858
But what about the gun?

76
00:05:17,442 --> 00:05:18,860
That hasn't been paid for yet.

77
00:05:21,112 --> 00:05:24,324
I could just make it
look like an accident.

78
00:05:26,951 --> 00:05:28,870
Are you really not going to stop?

79
00:05:28,953 --> 00:05:35,209
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES,
THEN FADES]

80
00:05:35,293 --> 00:05:37,628
[BILLY] Blaire,
please coordinate with Legal.

81
00:05:37,712 --> 00:05:41,340
I need a contract proposal
for Mr. Anthony on my desk.

82
00:05:41,424 --> 00:05:43,384
Please hurry. Thank you.

83
00:05:43,468 --> 00:05:44,761
- Go ahead. Bye!
- Bye, Billy.

84
00:05:45,386 --> 00:05:47,555
- Take care.
- [ENRICO] Oliver! Oliver! Oliver!

85
00:05:47,638 --> 00:05:49,348
- Oliver! Wait!
- [OLIVER] Why?

86
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:51,726
[PANTING]

87
00:05:51,809 --> 00:05:53,311
[ENRICO] Didn't I tell you

88
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:56,147
to never forget to take
your medicine with you?

89
00:05:56,981 --> 00:05:58,066
I'm sorry, Pa.

90
00:05:58,149 --> 00:05:59,233
Hmm.

91
00:05:59,317 --> 00:06:02,487
- Why did you leave it?
- [OLIVER] Billy, please don't be mad.

92
00:06:02,570 --> 00:06:07,158
Don't worry, when I get home,
I'll bring you a 100%!

93
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:08,534
What?

94
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:10,536
[OLIVER] We had an exam last week.

95
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:13,372
I'm sure that I scored a 100!

96
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:16,167
I did a good job for you!

97
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:19,670
Ever since you came back to us,

98
00:06:19,754 --> 00:06:25,176
I've become happier
and leveled up in my studying.

99
00:06:25,259 --> 00:06:28,471
Look at you! Are you really studying hard,
or are you fooling me?

100
00:06:28,554 --> 00:06:30,807
No, Pa! It's true. Promise!

101
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:32,600
[ENRICO CHUCKLES] Okay. Go ahead.

102
00:06:32,683 --> 00:06:34,185
[OLIVER] Bye, Billy. Thank you, Pa.

103
00:06:35,686 --> 00:06:37,522
- Take care, Oliver.
- Bye!

104
00:06:39,148 --> 00:06:40,024
Bye-bye!

105
00:06:46,697 --> 00:06:48,157
Are you all right?

106
00:06:49,117 --> 00:06:50,618
I'm okay. I'm fine, dear.

107
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:54,914
Dad?

108
00:06:54,997 --> 00:07:01,963
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

109
00:07:10,972 --> 00:07:12,223
What's taking so long?

110
00:07:12,306 --> 00:07:14,475
Where are our IDs and passports?

111
00:07:15,601 --> 00:07:17,103
Where's my gun first?

112
00:07:17,186 --> 00:07:19,605
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

113
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:20,982
[SIGHS]

114
00:07:22,316 --> 00:07:24,569
Surely Caloy told you why I took this.

115
00:07:24,652 --> 00:07:26,237
Your ID isn't ready yet.

116
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:28,698
What's taking so long? I can pay you.

117
00:07:28,781 --> 00:07:30,074
I'll get money from my son.

118
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:32,869
That's if

119
00:07:32,952 --> 00:07:34,370
he can still lend you some.

120
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:37,790
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

121
00:07:37,874 --> 00:07:39,167
What do you mean?

122
00:07:42,795 --> 00:07:43,880
Where's Caloy?

123
00:07:49,051 --> 00:07:51,137
[GRANADO] We just want to inform you that

124
00:07:51,679 --> 00:07:53,973
we will be filing
an Affidavit of Desistance

125
00:07:54,056 --> 00:07:56,684
with the Office of the Prosecutor
handling your case.

126
00:08:00,855 --> 00:08:01,814
Ah…

127
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:03,149
Desistance?

128
00:08:03,816 --> 00:08:07,069
[GRANADO] Ms. Cariño has already
withdrawn the charges against you.

129
00:08:08,571 --> 00:08:11,115
However, this is not
an automatic dismissal.

130
00:08:11,199 --> 00:08:14,035
It is still subject to
the evaluation of the prosecutor

131
00:08:14,118 --> 00:08:15,786
and will require clearance from the court.

132
00:08:18,164 --> 00:08:20,500
[CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY]

133
00:08:21,459 --> 00:08:22,418
Billy.

134
00:08:22,502 --> 00:08:24,295
Billy, thank you so much.

135
00:08:24,378 --> 00:08:26,422
Thank you so much.

136
00:08:28,382 --> 00:08:31,010
What about-- what about my mother?

137
00:08:31,093 --> 00:08:35,097
Will you withdraw the charges
against her too?

138
00:08:35,181 --> 00:08:41,812
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

139
00:08:41,896 --> 00:08:42,939
Billy.

140
00:08:43,648 --> 00:08:45,107
Billy, have mercy on my mom.

141
00:08:46,359 --> 00:08:50,947
Pursuant to the court's order
and following the psychiatric evaluation,

142
00:08:51,030 --> 00:08:53,783
your mother will be transferred
to hospital arrest.

143
00:08:55,493 --> 00:08:58,412
This may not be what my client wants, but…

144
00:08:58,496 --> 00:08:59,872
she will not contest.

145
00:09:01,082 --> 00:09:03,209
Hospital arrest?
[BREATH HITCHES]

146
00:09:03,292 --> 00:09:04,210
Hold on.

147
00:09:04,293 --> 00:09:07,088
[STUTTERING] My mother
won't be able to handle that.

148
00:09:07,171 --> 00:09:08,965
- [MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- She can't be on her own.

149
00:09:09,048 --> 00:09:10,758
Billy, she can't-- Pa.

150
00:09:12,426 --> 00:09:13,636
Bea.

151
00:09:13,719 --> 00:09:15,972
This is for your mother's own good.

152
00:09:16,055 --> 00:09:18,558
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

153
00:09:19,183 --> 00:09:20,226
Billy.

154
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:23,145
Billy, I'm begging you.

155
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:26,440
If you drop the case against my mom,

156
00:09:26,524 --> 00:09:29,110
I promise I'll watch over her.

157
00:09:29,193 --> 00:09:31,654
I promise she won't bother you.

158
00:09:31,737 --> 00:09:35,700
I promise, Billy. Please.
Just withdraw the case against my mother.

159
00:09:36,367 --> 00:09:37,451
Please, Billy. Please.

160
00:09:37,535 --> 00:09:39,453
Have mercy on my mother. Please.

161
00:09:40,079 --> 00:09:42,164
If you were in my position,

162
00:09:44,041 --> 00:09:48,129
and your family had almost died
because of someone…

163
00:09:50,965 --> 00:09:53,134
would you really let her walk free?

164
00:09:55,344 --> 00:09:59,515
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

165
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:02,184
Sorry.

166
00:10:03,894 --> 00:10:05,855
[STUTTERS] You're right, Billy.

167
00:10:05,938 --> 00:10:09,942
[TENSE MUSIC FADES]

168
00:10:10,026 --> 00:10:11,235
Thanks again.

169
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:17,908
Thank you for not pressing charges
against me.

170
00:10:17,992 --> 00:10:18,951
[BREATH HITCHES]

171
00:10:19,785 --> 00:10:21,037
Pa.

172
00:10:22,288 --> 00:10:29,295
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

173
00:10:41,557 --> 00:10:42,683
Thank you.

174
00:10:45,645 --> 00:10:52,151
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

175
00:11:02,536 --> 00:11:09,293
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

176
00:11:09,377 --> 00:11:11,545
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

177
00:11:12,546 --> 00:11:15,424
We've been with you
since the beginning, Anthony.

178
00:11:16,258 --> 00:11:18,761
Why aren't you renewing
your contract with us?

179
00:11:18,844 --> 00:11:20,721
- [MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- Billy, even if I wanted to,

180
00:11:20,805 --> 00:11:22,556
I don't have the final say right now.

181
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:25,059
<i>Then, who do I need to convince?</i>

182
00:11:25,142 --> 00:11:26,602
<i>Sir Gilbert?</i>

183
00:11:26,685 --> 00:11:29,188
<i>Set up a meeting.</i>
<i>I'll do the pitch myself.</i>

184
00:11:29,271 --> 00:11:32,233
Billy, Sir Gilbert already
wants to allocate

185
00:11:32,316 --> 00:11:34,151
the marketing funds somewhere else.

186
00:11:34,235 --> 00:11:37,780
[ANTHONY]<i> He thinks that there are better</i>
<i>advertising opportunities.</i>

187
00:11:39,031 --> 00:11:40,741
<i>Sorry to be very blunt.</i>

188
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:44,328
<i>Have a much more clear image</i>
<i>than LoveList right now.</i>

189
00:11:46,288 --> 00:11:48,374
<i>Billy, I'm sorry.</i>

190
00:11:48,457 --> 00:11:49,500
No, don't be.

191
00:11:49,583 --> 00:11:50,751
[CALL DISCONNECTS]

192
00:11:50,835 --> 00:11:53,963
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

193
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:57,341
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

194
00:11:57,425 --> 00:11:58,342
[BLAIRE] Chief?

195
00:11:58,426 --> 00:11:59,718
Chief, sorry to bother you.

196
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:01,804
The contractor called.

197
00:12:02,638 --> 00:12:07,977
Uh… they said your check bounced
for the down payment on the house rebuild.

198
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:11,772
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

199
00:12:11,856 --> 00:12:16,819
Didn't I tell you to remind me
to make the deposit?

200
00:12:16,902 --> 00:12:18,821
Yes, chief. I texted you the other day--

201
00:12:18,904 --> 00:12:21,657
[SHOUTING] You only texted me, Blaire!
You should've called me!

202
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:23,534
I'm sorry, chief.

203
00:12:23,617 --> 00:12:25,494
Chief, everyone's already
in the boardroom.

204
00:12:25,578 --> 00:12:27,746
- [KEYS JINGLING]
- [FOOTSTEPS RECEDING]

205
00:12:28,747 --> 00:12:34,170
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

206
00:12:46,974 --> 00:12:51,520
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES, FADES]

207
00:12:51,604 --> 00:12:56,734
Well, I suggest we launch with
influencer-led "real stories"

208
00:12:56,817 --> 00:12:58,611
type of campaign for the next quarter.

209
00:12:59,528 --> 00:13:00,529
Okay.

210
00:13:01,655 --> 00:13:04,575
Sorry, but with our budget,
can we hire a decent influencer?

211
00:13:04,658 --> 00:13:07,953
Plus, a "real story" type campaign?

212
00:13:08,037 --> 00:13:11,248
It's just gonna be obvious that
it's scripted. It's cringeworthy!

213
00:13:11,332 --> 00:13:13,918
[SARCASTICALLY] Oh, it is, is it?

214
00:13:14,543 --> 00:13:17,546
Well, at least I gave suggestions.

215
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:18,589
Did you?

216
00:13:19,173 --> 00:13:20,466
Wow, you just had to pick me out.

217
00:13:20,549 --> 00:13:22,134
At least I'm providing some feedback.

218
00:13:22,218 --> 00:13:25,137
Unlike some people who are busy
on their phone in the middle of a meeting.

219
00:13:25,221 --> 00:13:29,058
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

220
00:13:29,141 --> 00:13:31,810
Excuse me?
I've been messaging Val and Marj.

221
00:13:31,894 --> 00:13:33,604
They should've been here already.

222
00:13:33,687 --> 00:13:36,106
You know, I wish they were here,

223
00:13:36,190 --> 00:13:38,651
instead of the people
who shut down others' ideas

224
00:13:38,734 --> 00:13:40,653
but can't form one of their own.

225
00:13:40,736 --> 00:13:41,820
Are you targeting me?

226
00:13:41,904 --> 00:13:43,531
Why? Does the shoe fit?

227
00:13:44,156 --> 00:13:46,867
Guys, focus. Please.

228
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:49,995
We still have to come up with something
to present Billy.

229
00:13:50,079 --> 00:13:51,497
We're running out of time.

230
00:13:55,626 --> 00:14:02,424
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

231
00:14:04,552 --> 00:14:06,053
- [JORDAN] Dude--
- It's fine.

232
00:14:13,811 --> 00:14:15,563
- [CHARM] It's your fault!
- [TONI] That's right!

233
00:14:15,646 --> 00:14:16,730
[MORRIE] Why me?

234
00:14:24,196 --> 00:14:25,364
What is all this, huh?

235
00:14:25,447 --> 00:14:26,949
What is the meaning of this?

236
00:14:27,533 --> 00:14:29,201
- Bea, answer me.
- Ma…

237
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:34,331
Sir, can I talk with my mom privately
just for a few minutes?

238
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:36,375
Ma'am.

239
00:14:36,458 --> 00:14:38,210
- Let's head out for now.
- It won't take long.

240
00:14:40,629 --> 00:14:43,883
[WHISPERING] Ma… Ma, this is a blessing.

241
00:14:44,592 --> 00:14:45,634
This is a blessing!

242
00:14:45,718 --> 00:14:47,678
The assessment you got
from the doctor is good!

243
00:14:47,761 --> 00:14:50,598
[CRYING] They're bringing me
to a mental hospital!

244
00:14:50,681 --> 00:14:52,474
I'm not crazy!

245
00:14:52,558 --> 00:14:54,393
Of course not!

246
00:14:54,476 --> 00:14:56,103
I know you're not.

247
00:14:56,186 --> 00:15:00,316
[BEA] But… please don't complain.

248
00:15:00,941 --> 00:15:01,984
Because…

249
00:15:02,693 --> 00:15:05,613
[WHISPERING] Ma, they fell for our act.

250
00:15:07,031 --> 00:15:08,407
You know what?

251
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:11,827
Billy is dropping her charges against me.

252
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:13,621
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

253
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:14,997
How about me?

254
00:15:16,874 --> 00:15:18,792
I promise you, Ma.

255
00:15:18,876 --> 00:15:23,213
I will never stop begging Billy and Papa

256
00:15:23,297 --> 00:15:26,091
until I get you out of there. Okay?

257
00:15:27,134 --> 00:15:28,344
[MARIELA SNIFFLES]

258
00:15:28,427 --> 00:15:29,553
Ma…

259
00:15:30,638 --> 00:15:33,349
[BEA] Don't cry. Come on.

260
00:15:33,432 --> 00:15:35,392
All right, that's enough.

261
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:41,482
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

262
00:15:42,107 --> 00:15:47,071
[SNIFFLING]

263
00:15:50,991 --> 00:15:52,368
[SNIFFLES]

264
00:15:56,455 --> 00:15:58,999
[SNIFFLES, LIGHTLY WHIMPERING]

265
00:16:03,712 --> 00:16:04,880
[GULPS]

266
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:07,925
[CRYING]

267
00:16:10,177 --> 00:16:12,596
[SNIFFLING]

268
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:19,687
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

269
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:29,196
Your daughter couldn't say no to you.

270
00:16:29,279 --> 00:16:31,281
That's how much she loves you.

271
00:16:31,365 --> 00:16:33,325
When is Bea getting out?

272
00:16:33,409 --> 00:16:35,703
That depends on whether
the court approves of it.

273
00:16:35,786 --> 00:16:38,747
Until an official
court dismissal order is issued,

274
00:16:40,332 --> 00:16:41,875
she isn't allowed out.

275
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:44,545
Do you think Bea has truly changed?

276
00:16:44,628 --> 00:16:46,672
She made a promise to me.

277
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:48,841
Do you believe her?

278
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,593
I have to.

279
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:55,597
I have to help her.

280
00:16:55,681 --> 00:16:56,849
For her to change.

281
00:16:56,932 --> 00:17:03,772
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

282
00:17:05,357 --> 00:17:06,608
Dude.

283
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:08,110
Just relax.

284
00:17:08,193 --> 00:17:09,403
Okay?

285
00:17:09,486 --> 00:17:10,821
You're just stressed out.

286
00:17:10,904 --> 00:17:13,032
Jordan, of course I'm stressed!

287
00:17:13,115 --> 00:17:15,492
People's livelihoods are at stake here.

288
00:17:15,576 --> 00:17:19,747
And you want me to do what?
Go to your bar to chill?

289
00:17:20,414 --> 00:17:25,335
What I need to be okay are results.
Ideas to help the company.

290
00:17:25,419 --> 00:17:28,922
But everywhere I go,
all I hear about are problems!

291
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:30,883
So do you have any suggestions?

292
00:17:30,966 --> 00:17:33,302
Or are you too busy
with your side hustles?

293
00:17:33,385 --> 00:17:39,641
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

294
00:17:39,725 --> 00:17:40,893
Shit.

295
00:17:44,396 --> 00:17:45,355
Sorry, dude.

296
00:17:45,439 --> 00:17:46,523
Sorry, sorry.

297
00:17:49,109 --> 00:17:50,277
Dude.

298
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:54,156
I know you don't want to
drop the case against Bea.

299
00:17:54,239 --> 00:17:55,324
Okay?

300
00:17:59,369 --> 00:18:04,917
If I don't give Dad what he's asking for,
and something happens to him,

301
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:09,505
I'll carry that guilt
for the rest of my life.

302
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:15,094
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

303
00:18:15,177 --> 00:18:16,428
[CAR ENGINE STARTS]

304
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:18,097
[JORDAN] Can I make a suggestion?

305
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:21,016
Go home.

306
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,769
- Get some rest.
- Okay.

307
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:31,777
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

308
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:42,037
<i>A massive manhunt is underway</i>
<i>for the fugitives who escaped from prison.</i>

309
00:18:48,919 --> 00:18:50,254
<i>You're getting famous.</i>

310
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:53,507
<i>I have to warn Jordan.</i>

311
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:55,467
<i>You're acting like a hero.</i>

312
00:18:55,551 --> 00:18:56,802
<i>Are you getting anything in return?</i>

313
00:18:58,303 --> 00:18:59,346
<i>What?</i>

314
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:03,517
<i>Wait. What are you doing?</i>
<i>Where are you going?</i>

315
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:04,476
<i>Dino!</i>

316
00:19:10,691 --> 00:19:13,318
<i>Dad saved my life?</i>

317
00:19:22,035 --> 00:19:23,829
<i>Why are you here?</i>

318
00:19:24,413 --> 00:19:27,499
<i>Dude, I'm fine. You don't</i>
<i>have to check on me.</i>

319
00:19:28,125 --> 00:19:30,419
<i>I know it's busy at the bar right now.</i>

320
00:19:31,461 --> 00:19:32,713
<i>That's the thing, dude.</i>

321
00:19:33,338 --> 00:19:36,049
<i>It's too busy right now.</i>
<i>Too much noise.</i>

322
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:39,469
<i>I want to be somewhere quiet.</i>

323
00:19:40,429 --> 00:19:41,889
<i>I'm just getting stressed there.</i>

324
00:19:43,015 --> 00:19:44,433
<i>You're stressed?</i>

325
00:19:44,516 --> 00:19:46,518
[JORDAN EXHALES]

326
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:47,561
<i>I'm fine.</i>

327
00:19:47,644 --> 00:19:49,563
<i>Do you have a problem too?</i>

328
00:19:49,646 --> 00:19:52,107
<i>Dude, please don't worry about me.</i>

329
00:19:52,191 --> 00:19:53,275
<i>Okay?</i>

330
00:19:53,358 --> 00:19:55,444
<i>Right now, I just want</i>
<i>to be here with you.</i>

331
00:19:55,527 --> 00:19:56,820
<i>With me?</i>

332
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:59,198
<i>Maybe I can… stay here for now?</i>

333
00:19:59,281 --> 00:20:01,366
[GROANING]

334
00:20:01,450 --> 00:20:03,035
<i>Do you really not know</i>
<i>where Caloy is?</i>

335
00:20:03,118 --> 00:20:04,703
<i>Believe me.</i>

336
00:20:04,786 --> 00:20:06,830
<i>Believe me, Dino. I really don't know!</i>

337
00:20:06,914 --> 00:20:08,498
<i>If I learn that you're lying to me,</i>

338
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:09,625
<i>you're dead.</i>

339
00:20:09,708 --> 00:20:11,460
[CRYING] <i>Yes! Yes!</i>

340
00:20:11,543 --> 00:20:13,086
<i>You already know how to contact me.</i>

341
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:16,298
<i>If you hear anything about Caloy,</i>
<i>let me know right away.</i>

342
00:20:16,381 --> 00:20:17,633
<i>- Do you understand?</i>
<i>- Yes, yes!</i>

343
00:20:19,176 --> 00:20:20,802
- [JORDAN GRUNTS]
- [BILLY]<i> Jordan!</i>

344
00:20:20,886 --> 00:20:21,929
<i>What's happening?!</i>

345
00:20:22,012 --> 00:20:22,930
<i>Relax!</i>

346
00:20:23,513 --> 00:20:25,307
<i>- Relax, okay?</i>
<i>- Oh my God.</i>

347
00:20:25,974 --> 00:20:27,851
<i>Dude, I'm sorry.</i>

348
00:20:30,020 --> 00:20:32,522
<i>Are you okay? Huh?</i>

349
00:20:32,606 --> 00:20:36,193
<i>If you have a problem,</i>
<i>you can talk to me, okay?</i>

350
00:20:36,944 --> 00:20:38,654
<i>You look more stressed than me.</i>

351
00:20:39,279 --> 00:20:41,740
<i>Dude, I'm fine.</i>

352
00:20:44,451 --> 00:20:45,577
<i>Thank you.</i>

353
00:20:47,079 --> 00:20:48,497
<i>For letting me stay tonight.</i>

354
00:20:52,292 --> 00:20:53,961
<i>I know.</i>
[BEA SCOFFS]

355
00:20:54,044 --> 00:20:56,129
<i>You're all going to miss me!</i>

356
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:02,261
<i>Why? Are you sure that</i>
<i>you'll be able to get out?</i>

357
00:21:02,928 --> 00:21:04,388
<i>Absolutely.</i>

358
00:21:04,471 --> 00:21:06,181
<i>That's for sure.</i>

359
00:21:06,265 --> 00:21:07,766
<i>So if I were you,</i>

360
00:21:08,475 --> 00:21:10,644
<i>I'd behave myself</i>
<i>so I could get out too.</i>

361
00:21:10,727 --> 00:21:13,689
<i>Where are you going?</i>
<i>To a mental institution as well?</i>

362
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:17,276
<i>With your crazy mother?</i>

363
00:21:18,318 --> 00:21:20,112
<i>- What?!</i>
<i>- Who are you calling crazy?</i>

364
00:21:20,195 --> 00:21:23,573
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [HEAD THUDS]

365
00:21:23,657 --> 00:21:25,909
[OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]

366
00:21:25,993 --> 00:21:30,372
[INMATE SCREAMING]
<i>Somebody get help!</i>
